# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock is versioned on purpose: this crate is a binary, so the lockfile
# is what makes a build reproducible — and it is what pins the vendored
# rawloader patched in from Cargo.toml.

# Input data (camera RAW)
res*/
*.ARW
*.arw
*.CR2
*.CR3
*.NEF
*.RAF
*.ORF

# Image outputs
*.tif
*.tiff
*.dng
*.png
# The before/after images of comparison/ are deliberately NOT versioned: they
# are ~6 MB each and are regenerated from the output DNGs with the scripts in
# that directory (see comparison/README.md).

# Development sidecars (the ones in comparison/ are versioned)
/*.xmp

# Benchmarks and profiling
.bench/

# Logs
*.log

# System junk
.Trash-*/
.DS_Store
